# =============================================================================
#  MUMBAI 1:1 EXACT — data/sources.sha256
#
#  The canonical identity of every raw source the world is built from: sha256,
#  byte count, name.  It is committed (unlike data/raw/, which is ignored and
#  re-fetchable) so that a download is *verified* against a known-good file rather
#  than trusted, and so that a changed upstream is a loud failure instead of a
#  silently different city.
#
#  Provenance, licences and what each file contains: DOCS/01_DATA_SOURCES.md.
#  Checked by tools/fetch_data.sh — both after a download and in --verify-only
#  mode, which `make all-checks` runs.
#
#  Regenerating this file is a deliberate act: it means accepting whatever the
#  upstream now serves, and the consequences belong in DOCS/02_DECISIONS.md.
# =============================================================================
